# Workflow

## End of every task
- Never run `git commit` or `git push`. The developer commits.
- Finish with the exact commands, then what to do next. Keep every line short (a few paths per `git add`), never indent them, and end each line with `&&`, so a wrapped paste or a failed `git add` stops before the commit and push:
 ```bash
 git add <paths> &&
 git commit -m "feat(scope): what changed"
 ```

## Save tokens and time
- Never block on or poll long tasks (EAS builds, Docker builds on the VPS, deploys). Start them with `--no-wait`, or `nohup … > ~/.cache/grocery-build/<name>.log 2>&1 &`, or hand the command to the developer and ask for the result.
- Search with `rg`/Grep and read only what's needed. The generated Prisma client and `pnpm-lock.yaml` are kept out of the index; read `schema.prisma` instead.
- Keep progress notes to a sentence or two.
- When the conversation is long or the topic changes, suggest starting a new chat.

## Verification depth
- Copy, styling and small UI changes: typecheck and lint only.
- Money, auth, stock, orders, database, uploads, deploy config: full checks (see "Done means verified" in AGENTS.md).

## code-review-graph
Useful for reviewing large diffs (`detect_changes_tool`) and checking what a change affects. It can be stale and leaves many calls unresolved, so confirm exact checks with `rg`: every caller, every query returning a model, every use before a rename.
